WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.970
Two figures on an empty stage.

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.360
They step apart, and neither says a word.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:10.370
Byron's poem opens: "When we two parted".

4
00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:13.280
There are tears, and there is silence.

5
00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:14.750
Years pass.

6
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.680
Now a crowd whispers her name around him,

7
00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:19.520
and he says nothing.

8
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.040
Why would a poem about a
break-up keep going quiet?

9
00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:25.210
What is the speaker hiding?

10
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:29.580
In this mission, you'll trace how the
poem moves from that parting to the pain

11
00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.030
he feels now.

12
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:35.550
You'll hear how short, tight lines and a
strict rhyme scheme keep everything under

13
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.550
control.

14
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:42.260
And you'll ask why, after all that,
the poem ends "With silence and tears."

15
00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:45.650
Your mission: work out
what the speaker is hiding.
